WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.096
Hi! Where were you at the weekend?

2
00:00:06.496 --> 00:00:10.080
Today you learn the perfect tense with sein.

3
00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:15.975
Most verbs form the perfect tense with haben:

4
00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:18.783
I ate.

5
00:00:19.183 --> 00:00:22.671
But verbs of movement take sein:

6
00:00:23.071 --> 00:00:25.383
I went.

7
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:29.679
From A to B? Then sein!

8
00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.207
These verbs take sein:

9
00:00:34.607 --> 00:00:37.687
go: I went

10
00:00:38.087 --> 00:00:41.479
drive: I drove

11
00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:45.271
fly: I flew

12
00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:48.775
come: I came

13
00:00:49.175 --> 00:00:53.983
And an exception: stay, I stayed.

14
00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:59.803
With sein and haben we prefer war and hatte:

15
00:01:00.203 --> 00:01:02.635
I was at the cinema.

16
00:01:03.035 --> 00:01:05.107
Where were you?

17
00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:08.227
I had no time.

18
00:01:08.627 --> 00:01:10.963
You were lucky!

19
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:15.987
Listen: Mateo was away.

20
00:01:16.387 --> 00:01:19.251
Where were you at the weekend?

21
00:01:19.651 --> 00:01:22.083
I was in Hamburg.

22
00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:24.939
Did you fly?

23
00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:28.827
No, I went by train.

24
00:01:29.227 --> 00:01:31.467
And how was it?

25
00:01:31.867 --> 00:01:36.075
Great! I had lots of fun.

26
00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:46.175
Now you! Where were you last weekend? Where did you go?

27
00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:02.003
Great! Now you can:

28
00:02:02.403 --> 00:02:09.995
You know: movement from A to B takes sein. And war and hatte for sein and haben.

29
00:02:10.395 --> 00:02:12.515
See you soon!
